{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Strange Stories"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Useful Underwear of the Past"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe issues, in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social contexts. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le05ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Gerunds and Infinitives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <span class=\"strong\">gerund</span> is a verb ending with -ing (doing).<br/>An <span class=\"strong\">infinitive</span> is to + verb (to do)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by a gerund:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "report (doing)<br/>suceed in (doing)<br/>imagine (doing)<br/>spend time (doing)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">Who could <span class=\"strong\">imagine having</span> leather underwear?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You always use a gerund after a verb that is followed by a preposition.<br/><br/>Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The leather garment <span class=\"strong\">succeeded in sealing</span> the hole.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some verbs that can only be followed by an infinitive:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "used (to do)<br/>start (to do)<br/>begin (to do)<br/>able (to do)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Perhaps it hit a rock or was <span class=\"strong\">starting to</span> rot. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are some verbs that can be followed by an object plus an infinitive:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">The sailor took off his leather underwear and <span class=\"strong\">used it to</span> plug the hole.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The name Bronze Age is <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> classify prehistoric societies."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It <span class=\"strong\">began to</span> take on water. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They were <span class=\"strong\">able to</span> continue on to their destination."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They have <span class=\"strong\">reported finding</span> a leather undergarment in the side of the boat."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The archaeologists have <span class=\"strong\">spent</span> some <span class=\"strong\">time coming</span> up with a theory. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect vs. Simple Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br/><br/>You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past tense</span> to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span> to talk about experience.<br/>When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart about how to form the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>. Remember there are regular and irregular verbs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past tense form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"come\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"came\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"come\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Something has come to light.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" found\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" found\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Archeologists in England have found the wreckage of a Bronze Age boat. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" come across\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" came across\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" come across\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> To their surprise, they have come across something quite interesting.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" spend\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" spent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" spent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The archaeologists have spent some time coming up with a theory.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"plug\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"plugged\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"plugged\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The sailors have plugged the hole. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"travel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"travelled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"travelled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Have you ever travelled through the English Channel?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find a list of verbs and their past participle forms. Memorize as many as you can."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They have reported finding a leather undergarment in the side of the boat."}, {"type": "example", "content": "How did it get there you may ask?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "They were travelling through the English Channel when their boat got a hole in its side. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Perhaps it hit a rock or was starting to rot. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "It began to take on water. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "To stop the leak one of the sailors took off his leather underwear and used it to plug the hole."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Because water was no longer flowing into the boat they were able to continue on to their destination. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prehistoric"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to the time before written history"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The name Bronze Age is used to classify prehistoric societies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a surprising archaeological find."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "underwear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "clothing worn next to the skin under outer clothes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Not many people ever stop to wonder if people then wore underwear. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to come to light"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "to appear"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Something interesting has come to light."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fragment"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "a small piece"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Clothing fragments, if found, are rare."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wreckage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something damaged or destroyed "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Archaeologists in England have found the wreckage of a Bronze Age boat."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "undergarment"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an article of underwear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They have reported finding a leather undergarment in the side of the boat. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take on water"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fill with water through a hole in a boat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The boat began to take on water."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "supposition"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an assumption"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The most likely supposition is that they needed something to plug the hole."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to plug"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fill with something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To stop the leak one of the sailors took off his leather underwear and used it to plug the hole."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to seal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to close"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The leather garment succeeded in sealing the hole in the side of the boat until it was found last year."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le05ob07aud10"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go to the library or on the internet to find out about an archaeological find in your country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make some notes about: who found it, where, when, how, and where the find is now kept."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use your notes to write up your description using the Past Simple and Present Perfect tenses."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your description aloud to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find out about an archaeological find in your country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make notes on the find answering who, what, where, how."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the Past Simple and Present Perfect tenses to write the description."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your findings with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss coincidences, strange events or superstitions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about my attitudes toward an action."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about things that happened or have happened. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What artifacts from prehistory have 